I’m in a big room. It looks empty but it’s, in a way, full of things. Tiny things that complete the fragments. A lot of details. The blue doors stand out from the pale white wall, like two wooden totems. A white bike beside them, full of dried mood. Two coaches, I can barely see them because of the L shape of the room, but I know they’re there, like a lot of other things. We can sense them, I think. Two big windows near me cover one of the walls. They are open, I can see the blue sky, something strange for this city and for this time of the year. Two pairs of curtains, hanging there, like floating. Outside the trees are bare but the grass is green. Brick houses in line, one after another, everyone looks the same. Some cars, some people, some bikes from time to time. Three wardrobes, with different shapes, one in every corner -the corners that I can see- white, grey and dark, opened, messy, full of things. A tiny mirror on the floor, near the door. An old camera hanging from the same door. A circular and used dart target hanging. The sealing is white, made by rectangles, 1 x 2 rectangles, 95 of them. Three white tablets full of things, tiny things, strange things, like a workshop, it looks like if someone was using them, is using them. I think it could be too long to try to describe or name everything that is on the table, so I prefer not to. In the middle of the room there is a ghost sitting with its back on me.
The other room is smaller. Not too comfortable to write. I have to sit on the bed, that is just in the center of the room. The room is like a cube, almost a perfect one. 18 rectangles make the sealing. In one wall a blue door connects it to the other room. Beside it a dark stain on the wall, like a liquid drop. The other wall has a big windows with curtains and a heater, like before. Two more white, empty and little dirty walls. A wardrobe full of clothes in a corner. A plastic something in the other one. A metallic floor lamp in the third one, the last one is empty. This room, as I said, is smaller, and has some things but it feels empty, not used but dirty and a little messy. The double bed covers almost half of the floor, a grey doted floor. I’m in the bed. I can’t see myself, only my hands, writing here, and part of my striped t-shirt, white and blue, like a blanket that is covering me.
